# Ensure LF line endings for files consumed by include_str!() on all platforms.
# include_str!() preserves raw bytes; CRLF breaks substring assertions and
# produces different compiled binaries on Windows vs Linux/macOS. The explicit
# per-pattern eol=lf rules matter beyond `* text=auto`: with core.autocrlf=true
# a Windows checkout would otherwise materialize these files as CRLF.

* text=auto
*.md   text eol=lf
*.txt  text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.rhai text eol=lf
*.html text eol=lf
*.rs   text eol=lf

# git attributes are not retroactive: blobs committed with CRLF before these
# rules keep CRLF in the object database. One-time migration after adopting
# these rules (Git >= 2.16), then commit the result:
#   git add --renormalize .
